(6459859, 958927, 121949, '<td valign="top">Very cute little guy, but I''m not sure about the crop in this one, in my opinion it would be better either cropped closer or farther back to see more of the truck. Also this was taken at a slight angle from above, I think a lower angle more at his eye level would have been more effective. I would also like to see him either purposely looking away from the camera or looking strait at the camera. Sorry I don''t mean to be nit picky because otherwise this is a great shot, I guess I am just thinking out loud about what would take this shot from a good shot to a great shot.</td>', 'Very cute little guy, but I''m not sure about the crop in this one, in my opinion it would be better either cropped closer or farther back to see more of the truck. Also this was taken at a slight angle from above, I think a lower angle more at his eye level would have been more effective. I would also like to see him either purposely looking away from the camera or looking strait at the camera. Sorry I don''t mean to be nit picky because otherwise this is a great shot, I guess I am just thinking out loud about what would take this shot from a good shot to a great shot.', '2011-07-03 14:18:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459862, 958691, 121949, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting looking fan, I am thinking the main problem with this photo is the background IMO, as is I am left wondering why you chose to take a picture of a fan on a wall. When I set up a photograph I try to look at the picture as a whole, not just the subject, the background must add to the photo not detract. Try making a grouping of similar still life objects like propping it in front of a bonsai tree, or have a model hold the fan in front of her face, then you still showcase your beautiful fan, but the picture on a whole becomes much more interesting.</td>', 'This is an interesting looking fan, I am thinking the main problem with this photo is the background IMO, as is I am left wondering why you chose to take a picture of a fan on a wall. When I set up a photograph I try to look at the picture as a whole, not just the subject, the background must add to the photo not detract. Try making a grouping of similar still life objects like propping it in front of a bonsai tree, or have a model hold the fan in front of her face, then you still showcase your beautiful fan, but the picture on a whole becomes much more interesting.', '2011-07-03 14:28:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459864, 958272, 121949, '<td valign="top">Beautiful falls, but this photo has much more of a purple/red tint than sepia on my computer.</td>', 'Beautiful falls, but this photo has much more of a purple/red tint than sepia on my computer.', '2011-07-03 14:30:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459875, 958921, 121949, '<td valign="top">IMO this photo is too much about the gate instead of the child behind it. I would like to see this redone with the focus on the child instead of the gate. With the child out of focus it is hard to catch the emotion. I think if the child was moved to the left a bit so you can see the face it would be more effective as well. That heavy square over one of the eyes bothers me somewhat.</td>', 'IMO this photo is too much about the gate instead of the child behind it. I would like to see this redone with the focus on the child instead of the gate. With the child out of focus it is hard to catch the emotion. I think if the child was moved to the left a bit so you can see the face it would be more effective as well. That heavy square over one of the eyes bothers me somewhat.', '2011-07-03 14:36:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459879, 958314, 121949, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting looking clock, I am thinking the main problem with this photo is the background IMO, as is I am left wondering why you chose to take a picture of a clock on a blank wall. When I set up a photograph I try to look at the picture as a whole, not just the subject, the background must add to the photo not detract. Try making a grouping of similar still life objects like placing a nice flower arrangement with it on an interesting looking table. Then you still showcase your beautiful clock but make the picture as a whole much more interesting.</td>', 'This is an interesting looking clock, I am thinking the main problem with this photo is the background IMO, as is I am left wondering why you chose to take a picture of a clock on a blank wall. When I set up a photograph I try to look at the picture as a whole, not just the subject, the background must add to the photo not detract. Try making a grouping of similar still life objects like placing a nice flower arrangement with it on an interesting looking table. Then you still showcase your beautiful clock but make the picture as a whole much more interesting.', '2011-07-03 14:41:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459944, 958866, 20799, '<td valign="top">Simply and stunningly unbelievable. 10 from me. Yes there are some halos around the people but this is so 1868, who cares about some halos. I will be looking for this on the front page.</td>', 'Simply and stunningly unbelievable. 10 from me. Yes there are some halos around the people but this is so 1868, who cares about some halos. I will be looking for this on the front page.', '2011-07-03 16:39:08.000000', NULL, 1),
