(6463450, 958770, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nightpixels:</b></div><hr/><i> What a unique house with the kind of location it has.  Love this, Christophe!  It looks like your lens may have created some vignetting in the upper left corner of your image hence some noise? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks! The vignetting was created by the processing itself (HDR + curves to enhance blacks &amp; darks). I don''t think the lens created it in that case, since it wasn''t shifted at all. The noise was also due to the processing. Of course, I first removed it, but I liked this version more, as I felt it added some "vintage" feeling to it.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-07-06 16:10:53.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by nightpixels: What a unique house with the kind of location it has.  Love this, Christophe!  It looks like your lens may have created some vignetting in the upper left corner of your image hence some noise?   Thanks! The vignetting was created by the processing itself (HDR + curves to enhance blacks & darks). I don''t think the lens created it in that case, since it wasn''t shifted at all. The noise was also due to the processing. Of course, I first removed it, but I liked this version more, as I felt it added some "vintage" feeling to it.', '2011-07-06 17:09:32.000000', '2011-07-06 17:10:53.000000', 0),
