(6546455, 958235, 124982, '<td valign="top">Just saw this now, quite a wonderful image!! The processing on this is perfect for the image, exceptionally dark and moody. Especially appreciate the toning as opposed to straight B&amp;W. Very nice!</td>', 'Just saw this now, quite a wonderful image!! The processing on this is perfect for the image, exceptionally dark and moody. Especially appreciate the toning as opposed to straight B&W. Very nice!', '2011-09-20 23:23:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6556353, 958557, 29011, '<td valign="top">Beautiful work. It''s an instant fave to me! It''s perfect for Sephia. The added warmth adds a whole other feel to the shot.</td>', 'Beautiful work. It''s an instant fave to me! It''s perfect for Sephia. The added warmth adds a whole other feel to the shot.', '2011-10-01 00:56:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(6620818, 958927, 30982, '<td valign="top">Entirely too cute.  But oh what a serious look your subject has!  Timothy''s comment is quite appropriate.</td>', 'Entirely too cute.  But oh what a serious look your subject has!  Timothy''s comment is quite appropriate.', '2011-12-18 16:24:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(6620842, 958927, 61084, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> Entirely too cute.  But oh what a serious look your subject has!  Timothy''s comment is quite appropriate. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, he does have a serious look, and in other shots he is smiling more. His expression here is one of the big reasons why I chose to use this shot though. It''s a very serious and dry expression, but when I was taking the shot I knew I wanted to do a kind of vintage "Spanky and Our Gang" look. I don''t know with the hat and truck it just reminded me of the Little Rascals and the expression seemed appropriate. LOL.<br/> <br/>I love all the comments I''ve gotten on this shot. Thanks to all, and once again thank you to you Deb. :)<br/> <br/>Dave</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: Entirely too cute.  But oh what a serious look your subject has!  Timothy''s comment is quite appropriate.   Yes, he does have a serious look, and in other shots he is smiling more. His expression here is one of the big reasons why I chose to use this shot though. It''s a very serious and dry expression, but when I was taking the shot I knew I wanted to do a kind of vintage "Spanky and Our Gang" look. I don''t know with the hat and truck it just reminded me of the Little Rascals and the expression seemed appropriate. LOL. I love all the comments I''ve gotten on this shot. Thanks to all, and once again thank you to you Deb. :) Dave', '2011-12-18 17:01:05.000000', NULL, 0),
